WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Let's explore how we can create a new

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.200
page in hacks.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.519
The top corner I can see this blue

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:13.360
button that says add page.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.240
Clicking add page will prompt the search

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.760
bar so that I can type the page title to

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.080
create a new page or I can just hit

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.720
enter to create a page with a title new

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.320
page.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.800
Let's name this

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.680
given text.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.760
I can use the keyboard navigate between

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.840
the options if I want to duplicate the

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.960
current page or create a blank one. So,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.640
let's create a blank one.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.360
Notice that the slug or this part of the

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.719
URL that goes beyond the name of our

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:54.960
site says given hyphen text. Also, the

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.079
title reflects this with given text. But

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:01.280
I could change it after the fact if I

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.239
needed to.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:06.880
I can edit different details about this

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.520
page by clicking the select to edit page

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.479
details in the body of the content. So

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:15.680
if I were to do some writing,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.799
maybe add an image via slash commands,

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:20.640
build out video, what have you, and say,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.400
"Oh no, that I need to change the

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.080
title." I can go select page, right?

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.640
There's the given text. After the fact,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.520
I could go under advance and modify this

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.079
part of the slug or URL if I needed.

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:36.479
Change the publishing status, lock this

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:39.360
page, move it around in the outline, and

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.200
there's some more advanced operations as

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.200
well. But for now, I'll just hit save.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.520
Right. So, we have our updated page text

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.840
and title.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.479
Some other areas that I can use to add a

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.520
page would be under

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.320
the outline actions. So if I'm

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.840
overworking with this part of the

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.920
outline, then I could click add child

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.600
page and I would get the same

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.640
interactive pattern as above. In this

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.440
case, I'll just hit enter. You see we

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.879
get a new page here. I'll hit save.

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:15.920
However, this one is underneath the

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.440
given text after the fact page.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.760
So this is a easy way to add a child

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.000
page whereas this is just going to add a

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
page wherever you are in the hierarchy.
